## Context

Upstream issue #43 (filed 2026-08-31 by a third party, not the maintainer)
asks for `ZOTEUS_LOCAL_EMBEDDING_MODEL=<hf-id>` so users can point the local
embedder at a different transformers.js model, motivated by German/multilingual
retrieval, and names `Xenova/multilingual-e5-small`. As literally proposed it
swaps only the model string: `LocalEmbeddingProvider.embed()`
(`fork/src/features/search/embeddings.ts:258`) hardcodes
`{ pooling: 'mean', normalize: true }` and applies no input-template prefix,
so a naive implementation of #43 would silently mis-pool or mis-normalize any
model that isn't MiniLM, and would embed E5 models with no `"query: "`/
`"passage: "` prefix -- the exact defect this repo's own registry work exists
to prevent (0488's ladder). The author asked for a substantive comment on #43,
not a light courtesy note: share the registry design, the measured evidence
behind it, the code points, and a staged rollout -- enough for someone else to
implement it correctly, without leaking this repo's internal governance
(GOVERNANCE.md's disclosure rule).

## Relevant files

- `fork/src/features/search/embeddings.ts` -- `LocalEmbeddingProvider`
  (model default line 186, hardcoded pooling/normalize line 258),
  `embedderIdentity()` (line 29, the existing vector-space-mismatch hook),
  `createEmbeddingProvider()` (line 393, constructs the local provider with no
  model argument -- `ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL` is wired to API providers only)
- `bench/models.json` -- the registry schema and the 21 candidates already
  probed for ONNX availability
- `tickets/0266-cross-lingual-probe-on-the-multilingual.erg` (closed) --
  the cross-lingual measurement with controls
- `tickets/0495-gate-which-embedder-entries-ship.erg` -- the per-passage
  build-time figures
- `tickets/0488-deliver-curated-embedder-registry-invari.erg` and its children
  -- the registry ladder this comment summarizes

## Actions

1. Draft the comment text as a standalone file, upstream-formatting
   conventions (decimal point, no internal ticket/document names, no
   governance references), citing only code points and measured evidence.
2. Self-review against the actual sources above -- every number and every
   file:line must be re-verified, not recalled, per this repo's own drafting
   discipline (see 0024's log on the two defects caught in the I-3 review
   pass).
3. Present the draft to the author for content sign-off before anything is
   posted -- posting to a public upstream thread is an outward action that
   needs explicit authorization each time (CLAUDE.md).

